# Cleanup

Canonical source: `skills/cleanup/SKILL.md`.

## When To Use

- Review ready passed and the slice can close.
- User asks to wrap up, sync docs, or clean state.
- Multiple plans/specs look authoritative (dual truth).

## Inputs

- `skills/cleanup/SKILL.md`, AGENTS/README/docs, recovery Work Index, plans/specs that still look live, git status.

## Procedure

1. Name the one work surface (Work Index active primary artifact).
2. Compare living docs to code.
3. Archive or status-mark superseded plans/specs; clear or defer entropy.
4. Small living-doc fixes; regenerate generated artifacts via generators only.
5. Report closure state and Next.

## Outputs

- CLEANUP report with work surface, archive/deferred, git summary.

## Verification / Done Criteria

- One work surface named or blocker recorded.
- Entry points do not treat replaced plans as current.
- Uncertain files not silently deleted.
